{"qid":"Q222","names":["Albania","Republic of Albania"],"title":"Albania","endonym":{"native":"Republika e Shqipërisë","lang":"sq"},"capsule":"Albania declared independence from the Ottoman Empire on 28 November 1912 at Vlorë, with Ismail Qemali leading the proclamation, ending five centuries of Ottoman rule. The interwar period saw brief attempts at a republic (1925–1928) under Fan Noli, then a monarchy under Ahmet Zogu, who declared himself King Zog I. Italian forces invaded in April 1939 and Albania became a protectorate; German occupation followed in 1943. The People's Republic was proclaimed in January 1946 under Enver Hoxha's communist partisans, closing the monarchical period.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Albania's borders from 1912 onward are well attested through treaty records (London 1913, post-WWI settlements), though the precise delimitation shifted considerably in 1913–1921 and remains contested at the edges.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Albania","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albania"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Ismail Qemali","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ismail_Qemali"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Zog I of Albania","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zog_I_of_Albania"},{"label":"Wikipedia: People's Republic of Albania","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People%27s_Republic_of_Albania"}],"britannica":"place/Albania","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Albania","rulers":[{"qid":"Q46932","name":"Ismail Kemal","start":1912,"end":1914,"image":"Ismail Kemal Bey.png","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ismail%20Kemal%20Bey.png?width=320","imageLicen